! The symmetry-reduced twin of `pt-soc-paw-nosym.in`: the same input with `nosym` and
! `noinv` removed and nothing else changed, the unshifted 2x2x2 grid kept, so that
! the k-set is the irreducible wedge of the grid `pt-soc-paw-nosym.in` runs whole.
!
! It exists for the j-resolved projection's group average, `sym_proj_so`: the
! wedge's symmetrised Loewdin charges, column by column, have to reproduce the
! closed grid's, which `pt-soc-paw-nosym.in` checks against `projwfc.x` itself
! (`reference.projwfc.pt-soc-paw`, `lsym = .false.`).
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 7.42, nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    lspinorb = .true.,
    noncolin = .true.,
    starting_magnetization = 0.0,
    occupations = 'smearing',
    degauss = 0.02,
    smearing = 'mp',
    ecutwfc = 30.0,
    ecutrho = 250.0,
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0e-8
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
Pt  195.08   Pt.rel-pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS {alat}
Pt  0.0000000   0.00000000   0.0
K_POINTS AUTOMATIC
2 2 2 0 0 0
